THE GREAT EMU WAR
An "Under 7 Minutes" episode

Written, directed, animated and scored in code with the Lemo-Opuscar library (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar).

Narration and character voices: Kokoro-82M text-to-speech (Apache-2.0), voices bm_george, am_michael, bm_daniel, bm_lewis.
Music: original score, played on samples from VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios), CC0.
Sound effects: synthesised in code (core/audio/sfx.py).
Typeface: Inter Tight by Rasmus Andersson and contributors, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL-intertight.txt).

History notes: the operation ran from November to December 1932 in the Campion district of Western Australia, under
Major G. P. W. Meredith of the Royal Australian Artillery. Numbers in the film follow the commonly cited figures
(about 20,000 emus, ~10 rounds per confirmed kill, 57,034 bounties claimed in six months of 1934); sources disagree on
some of them.

Character designs, the emu, the title card and the refrain are original to this film.
